==Strategy==
This stage is easily won by bringing 3-4 meatshields, 1-2 midranged area attackers ([[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Figure Skating Cats]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|C. Legs]], etc.) and 2-3 long-ranged attackers ([[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|C. Dragon]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|C. Bahamut]], etc.).

Start by stalling Norn with Wall Cats until Serum comes out, and then send a few of your midrangers until your units reach the enemy base. During this phase, make sure you build up your [[Worker Cat]] to at least level 4. When you reach the base, you should have enough money to start sending out your heavy hitters and a couple of long-ranged attackers. Keep sending meatshields and attackers when you have enough money. You should win if your Cats are at sufficient levels (at least level 25-30 but can be less for Legend units).

